+RULING 1 — E6: Coverage-Disclosed Dynasty Scoring
+
+E6 is ratified as drafted, Option a: no official rankings across different coverage profiles.
+
+1. Missing-axis weights remain in abeyance. No redistribution, ever, without explicit owner ratification (AA10). This supersedes the Annex B renormalize clause in full.
+2. Every score emission reports, as distinct fields: coverage · observed weighted average · weighted subtotal (average × coverage) · missing axes · formula version · raw per-axis values. A partial score is never represented as complete.
+3. Official comparisons require identical formula version AND identical coverage profile. Observed averages may be computed for internal analysis; they are not official rankings.
+4. Historical scores are immutable. No retroactive completeness.
+5. Scoring is deterministic (same journal + formula version → byte-identical emission) and journal-derived only. Proposals, predictions, self-reports, and observer interpretations are not evidence.
+6. The observer is read-only and permission-blind: scores never influence action validation; no observer output becomes world-truth. (CI import-graph restriction to follow in the RG mapping.)
+⟪AMENDMENT F-01 — exact semantics, replaces any ambiguity in Ruling 1 items 2–3⟫
+Formal definition. Each axis value x_i is the Annex B pipeline output (min-max normalized, square-root diminished) for present axes only. Let W = {.25 survival, .20 successors, .20 territory, .20 artifacts, .15 wealth}. For present set P:
+- coverage c = Σ{i∈P} w_i
+- raw weighted sum s = Σ{i∈P} w_i·x_i
+- observed weighted average = s / c  (a conditional descriptive statistic; original weights are preserved in both s and c — the full-W denominator is NEVER used, so observed average and subtotal remain distinct quantities)
+- weighted subtotal = s  (≡ observed average × c)
