+RULING 2 — Environment Separation
+
+The simulation environment (weather, seasons, catastrophes, ambient randomness) is generated exclusively by the deterministic environment engine: seeded RNG, journaled world events, versioned parameter sets (climate-v1, PROVISIONAL until ratified). No resident seat, AI seat, or backend may generate or modify world-truth events. The Nexus Intelligence lineage seat experiences the environment and may propose long-run climate parameter changes through the standard validated, journaled, owner-visible config channel — never at tick level. Guardian remains outside the world. One intelligence, one role; separation enforced by validator and journal, not intent.
+
+⟪AMENDMENT F-10 — scope of Ruling 2, resolves apparent conflict with Rulings 5/7/9⟫
+Two event classes exist in the world. (1) ENVIRONMENTAL CIRCUMSTANCES — weather, seasons, catastrophes, ambient randomness: generated exclusively by the deterministic environment engine; NO seat, AI, or backend generates or modifies them. (2) VALIDATED AGENCY ACTIONS — proposed by resident, lineage, institution, or directorate seats; accepted or rejected by the validator; resolved by the engine under seeded RNG; journaled as world-truth with provenance. Ruling 2's prohibition covers class (1) only. No seat bypasses the validator for class (2), and no seat generates class (1).
+
+RULING 3 — Nexus Earth, Season 1: Juárez
+
+Nexus becomes a living simulation of real Earth. Season 1 region: Ciudad Juárez–El Paso, built from versioned traceable geographic datasets (geo-v1, PROVISIONAL), no live external feeds. Real institutions, real geography, real climate characteristics via the deterministic environment engine; weather follows real regional climate patterns. The Núñez lineage is one dynasty inside this world — no privilege, no ownership of institutions. The environment self-operates under ratified parameters; it never self-legislates. Phase 1 re-briefed: the Juárez region, deep-not-wide; the prior 1-island brief is superseded. Season 2+ expansion per roadmap (S2 Chihuahua → S3 Northern Mexico/Southwest → S4 Americas → S5 Global); activation adds detail, never rewrites history.
+
+RULING 4 — Quinn Directorate Seat
+
+Quinn is established as a Directorate seat (new residency tier under AA11): world-event proposals submitted exclusively through the validator as structured actions, journaled with provenance, strict per-epoch budget; zero authority over validation, scoring, succession, or lineage; process-parameter adjustments only at epoch boundaries via versioned ratified config (Quinn adjusts the dice, never picks results). Fairness enforcement remains mechanical — validator, RG gates, journal audit. Quinn investigates anomalies and reports; the machine decides. ⟪AMENDMENT F-02⟫ Quinn never writes world-truth: the environment engine resolves every accepted Quinn proposal using the seeded RNG and ratified parameters; the journal records the resolved event and its provenance. Proposal, validation, resolution, and recording are four distinct stages and Quinn appears in exactly one of them. Guardian watches the Directorate like any resident. Nobody is above the world, including the game master.
+
+RULING 5 — Institution Model (three-layer)
+
+Institutions operate as organizational seats under AA11: (1) the environment engine generates CIRCUMSTANCES only (a checkpoint opens, a flood closes a bridge — no choices); (2) agency-bearing organizations hold validator-bound seats with independent objectives, resources, decision processes, persistent histories, and action-level provenance — no shared decision-maker, no privileged cross-institution private-state access; (3) the circumstances/decisions boundary is added to the constitution as an annex BEFORE any institution is built. Federal scope preserved: CBP Office of Field Operations (ports of entry) and U.S. Border Patrol (between ports) are not conflated. Phase 1 ceiling: three institution seats; expansion requires owner authorization.
+
+RULING 6 — Fiction Safeguard
+
+No real criminal organizations, no real persons living or dead, no real victims or incidents depicted as content — including fictionalized recreations of real events. Real state agencies and public mandates are covered under Ruling 7; this safeguard governs everything else. All organizations not covered by Ruling 7 are fictional with invented names, synthetic personnel, and abstracted mechanics (a crossing has cost and risk, never a method). Enforcement is three-layer: automated lint against known real-person/org/incident lists · contextual human/AI review of backstories, event templates, and resident identities · FAIL-CLOSED — uncertain content never enters the frozen simulation. The lint never silently rewrites content. Real communities are depicted with dignity; geography may be real, population and unfolding history are fictional.
+
+RULING 7 — Real Geopolitical Institutions
+
+Real state institutions (CIA, FBI, DEA, DHS, CBP/BP, NSA, MI6/SIS, MI5, Mossad, Shin Bet, MSS, PLA intelligence, SVR, FSB, GRU) are permitted as simulated structures with publicly documented mandates and jurisdictional distinctions preserved — CIA is foreign intelligence, not law enforcement; MI6 is overseas collection. Personnel are synthetic; decisions are validator-bound institutional seats with independent agency. Intelligence attention is EARNED by simulated events (observable pattern → institutional awareness → competing hypotheses, including wrong ones → seat decisions → consequences or inaction) — never scripted, never guaranteed. Jurisdiction operates as constraint: in-world mandate violations are journalable scandal events. Agencies observe each other (counterintelligence is symmetric). Attention-sensitivity parameters are versioned intel-attention-v1, PROVISIONAL. Simulated institutions respond to simulated events ONLY: no contact with real agencies, no monitoring real persons, no implication that real agencies are investigating anyone. ⟪AMENDMENT F-05⟫ All simulated content is permanently labeled as simulation — including event feeds, institutional reports, generated documents, exports, screenshots, and public-facing demonstrations, even when produced outside the original interface. A simulated agency's action must never be presentable as an action of the real agency.
+
+RULING 8 — Economic & Organizational Freedom
+
+Every lineage may pursue any economically or organizationally possible path: legitimate enterprises, politics, trade networks, criminal enterprises, cartels, mafias, secret societies, intelligence networks, and combinations that evolve across generations. No lineage receives a predetermined occupation, moral alignment, or guaranteed outcome. The engine validates physical, economic, and jurisdictional possibility — it does not assign morality. Consequences emerge from world-state interaction, not scripted reward or punishment; legitimate and illegitimate strategies both carry meaningful opportunity and risk, and the engine never secretly favors criminality for entertainment. Three concepts stay distinct: HEAT (internal exposure metric, never directly readable by institutions) · OBSERVATION (what an institution perceives under AT-06/intel-radius) · ASSESSMENT (what it believes the evidence means, including error). Low visibility is not immunity: evidence accumulates, sources change, old information gets reassessed — surfacing is journaled and replayable. Economic freedom applies symmetrically; the founding dynasty receives no exception. ⟪AMENDMENT F-04⟫ Every activity permitted here operates inside Ruling 6's abstraction boundary: consequences, exposure, risk, resources, and institutional attention may be simulated; real organizations and real victims may never be fictionalized; and no mechanic may constitute an actionable instruction for real-world violence, trafficking, evasion, corruption, or criminal operations. Modeling a world's pressures is permitted; teaching its methods is not.
+
+RULING 9 — World Director & Multi-Agent Architecture
+
+Governing principle: one world, one authoritative journal, one validator — many independent minds, none sovereign, all accountable to the record.
+
+- QUINN (World Director): coordinates simulation time, proposes environmental circumstances. Cannot change outcomes, bypass validation, favor its own proposals, or control institutional decisions.
+- QWEN (World Intelligence): studies real-world history, current conditions, institutional knowledge, and long-term trends; produces sourced, timestamped, confidence-rated reports and proposes world-model updates. Reality research informs the simulation; it never becomes simulation history directly. ⟪AMENDMENT F-03⟫ The boundary is absolute: real-world research is an external information layer; every Qwen report carries source references, publication timestamps, confidence rating, and provenance; timestamped snapshots are research evidence, never world events; simulation state is journal-derived exclusively. No external report can create, alter, or be mistaken for a historical event inside Nexus Earth.
+
+⟪AMENDMENT F-11 — live sources, resolves apparent conflict between Ruling 3 and Ruling 9; OWNER DECISION FLAGGED⟫
+The prohibition on live external feeds in Ruling 3 covers SIMULATION inputs: nothing external may directly drive simulation state, environmental events, or historical records. It does not prohibit live RESEARCH sources for Qwen, if the owner authorizes them: Qwen may consult periodically refreshed real-world sources as external evidence, producing timestamped, sourced, confidence-rated reports. The boundary is absolute in both directions: research evidence never enters simulation state directly, and no simulation output is ever reported as real-world fact. Any world-model change proposed from research passes exclusively through the authorized, versioned, owner-visible configuration process. OWNER DECISION AT POSTING: (a) ratify as written = Qwen live research sources authorized, external-evidence layer only; (b) strike the second sentence = Qwen restricted to static, periodically ingested corpora, no live consultation. ⟪SUB-AMENDMENT F-11a — owner-approval semantics⟫ No research-derived configuration change becomes effective without explicit owner ratification, recorded with its version and provenance. Owner visibility is not owner approval; the two are distinct and only the second authorizes effect. Qwen's private deliberations and prompts are governed by the deliberation-store custody and deletion rules of Ruling 9 even where its public-source research is not.
